  "question": {
    "text": "Let the refractive index of a denser medium with respect to rarer medium be <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub></math> and its critical angle be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math> . At an angle of incidence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> when light is travelling from denser medium to rarer medium, a part of the light is reflected and the rest is refracted and the angle between reflected and refracted rays is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>.&nbsp;Angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;"
  },
